{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110765","id":2847618596,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6puzYk","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110765","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110765.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110765.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110765","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110765/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110765/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110765/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/5e6831d640b7859a115a6aeecc4b405babcb26a4","number":110765,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add NoiseTextureGenerator singleton","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds `NoiseTextureGenerator` singleton to facilitate the baking of noise textures using existing threads from the `WorkerThreadPool` when available.\r\n\r\nPreviously each single `NoiseTexture2D/3D` created its own dedicated `Thread`, which was neither efficient or performant.\r\n\r\nThis fresh thread creation made it more or less performance impossible to use noise textures at runtime when not hidden behind a loading screen. The thread-spawn alone would cause stutters to no end on all platforms with a higher thread-spawn costs like Windows. Having so many additional threads running next to the actual WorkerThreadPool max thread count caused a lot of thread congestion when many noise textures were used.\r\n\r\nThis PR removes the dedicated `Thread` from `NoiseTexture2D/3D` and makes them use `WorkerThreadPool` threads to bake noise images. Because this requires additional bookkeeping and thread synchronization work a new `NoiseTextureGenerator` singleton was added.\r\n\r\nNote that there is no elegant hook option with the main loop to do thread synchronization for optional modules like the noise module. To solve this I decided to piggyback on the RenderingServer `frame_pre_draw` signal for thread synchronization. The reason I did not pick a SceneTree signal for this (like some other resources and nodes do) is because not every main loop is always a SceneTree, so those signals might not be available at all.\r\n\r\nUsing the `frame_pre_draw` signal also allows to sync all the noise bakes that users kicked off in script and that might have been finished quickly by the time the RenderingServer starts its own sync and frame thing. This gives less window to run into issues with async baked noise textures being already baked so the duplicated bake attempts get blocked. Keeping the wait window small is important because all the noise resources have this awkward implementation of using the deferred queue for auto updates that users can't really stop from triggering.\r\n\r\nNote that this largely copies the bake logic of the navigation mesh generator, except for the new signal and deferred quirks that are specific to the noise module and resources.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/code_style.html\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1007033697,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDA3MDMzNjk3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/salvageable","name":"salvageable","description":"","color":"ff7766","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-09-22T01:29:27Z","updated_at":"2025-11-08T23:25:27Z","closed_at":"2025-11-08T23:25:19Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"9466e9da0f7b0e4df7ba551c68b19bc8ffc19cee","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"smix8:noise_gen","ref":"noise_gen","repo":{"id":358277329,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkzNTgyNzczMjk=","name":"godot","full_name":"smix8/godot","owner":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api